        "title": "Introduction",
        "key_prerequisites": [],
        "has_content_in_snapshot": true,
        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Let&#x27;s consider the following expression:</p>",
            "readable_text": "Let's consider the following expression:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 12\\div 4 \\times 7]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: 12\\div 4 \\times 7]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Notice that this expression contains multiplication <em>and</em> division. So how do we compute its value?</p>",
            "readable_text": "Notice that this expression contains multiplication and division. So how do we compute its value?",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>To help us, we have the following rule: </p>",
            "readable_text": "To help us, we have the following rule:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<blockquote><p><em>When an expression contains only multiplication and division, we carry out the operations from left to right</em>.</p></blockquote>",
            "readable_text": "> When an expression contains only multiplication and division, we carry out the operations from left to right.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>So, we must first carry out the division <span class=\"math\">[MATH: (12\\div 4).]</span> We can emphasize this using parentheses <span class=\"math\">[MATH: (\\phantom{0}){:}]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "So, we must first carry out the division [MATH: (12\\div 4).] We can emphasize this using parentheses [MATH: (\\phantom{0}){:}]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\big(12\\div 4\\big) \\times 7]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: \\big(12\\div 4\\big) \\times 7]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Here, the parentheses tell us which part of the expression to do first.</p>",
            "readable_text": "Here, the parentheses tell us which part of the expression to do first.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Now, we evaluate our expression as follows:</p>",
            "readable_text": "Now, we evaluate our expression as follows:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: (12 \u00f7 4) \u00d7 7|=; 3 \u00d7 7|=; 21]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: (12 \u00f7 4) \u00d7 7|=; 3 \u00d7 7|=; 21]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nLet's consider the following expression:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 12\\div 4 \\times 7]\n\nContent:\nNotice that this expression contains multiplication and division. So how do we compute its value?\n\nContent:\nTo help us, we have the following rule:\n\nContent:\n> When an expression contains only multiplication and division, we carry out the operations from left to right.\n\nContent:\nSo, we must first carry out the division [MATH: (12\\div 4).] We can emphasize this using parentheses [MATH: (\\phantom{0}){:}]\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\big(12\\div 4\\big) \\times 7]\n\nContent:\nHere, the parentheses tell us which part of the expression to do first.\n\nContent:\nNow, we evaluate our expression as follows:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: (12 \u00f7 4) \u00d7 7|=; 3 \u00d7 7|=; 21]"
      },
