        "title": "Swapping Multiplication and Division",
        "key_prerequisites": [],
        "has_content_in_snapshot": true,
        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Let&#x27;s now consider the following expression:</p>",
            "readable_text": "Let's now consider the following expression:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 10{\\color{red}{\\,\\div\\, 6\\,}} {\\color{blue}{\\,\\times\\, 3}}]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: 10{\\color{red}{\\,\\div\\, 6\\,}} {\\color{blue}{\\,\\times\\, 3}}]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>We carry out the operations from left to right. However, the division problem is difficult because <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 10]</span> cannot be divided evenly into groups of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 6.]</span> So, what do we do?</p>",
            "readable_text": "We carry out the operations from left to right. However, the division problem is difficult because [MATH: 10] cannot be divided evenly into groups of [MATH: 6.] So, what do we do?",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>To help us, we have the following rule:</p>",
            "readable_text": "To help us, we have the following rule:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<blockquote><p><em>When the only operations are multiplication and division, we can swap the order in which the operations are carried out.</em></p></blockquote>",
            "readable_text": "> When the only operations are multiplication and division, we can swap the order in which the operations are carried out.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Therefore, we can swap the order of the multiplication and division as follows:</p>",
            "readable_text": "Therefore, we can swap the order of the multiplication and division as follows:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 10{\\color{blue}{\\,\\times\\, 3}}{\\color{red}{\\,\\div\\, 6\\,}}]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: 10{\\color{blue}{\\,\\times\\, 3}}{\\color{red}{\\,\\div\\, 6\\,}}]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Now, we evaluate our expression:</p>",
            "readable_text": "Now, we evaluate our expression:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 10 \u00d7 3 \u00f7 6|=; (10 \u00d7 3) \u00f7 6|=; 30 \u00f7 6|=; 5]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: 10 \u00d7 3 \u00f7 6|=; (10 \u00d7 3) \u00f7 6|=; 30 \u00f7 6|=; 5]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nLet's now consider the following expression:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 10{\\color{red}{\\,\\div\\, 6\\,}} {\\color{blue}{\\,\\times\\, 3}}]\n\nContent:\nWe carry out the operations from left to right. However, the division problem is difficult because [MATH: 10] cannot be divided evenly into groups of [MATH: 6.] So, what do we do?\n\nContent:\nTo help us, we have the following rule:\n\nContent:\n> When the only operations are multiplication and division, we can swap the order in which the operations are carried out.\n\nContent:\nTherefore, we can swap the order of the multiplication and division as follows:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 10{\\color{blue}{\\,\\times\\, 3}}{\\color{red}{\\,\\div\\, 6\\,}}]\n\nContent:\nNow, we evaluate our expression:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 10 \u00d7 3 \u00f7 6|=; (10 \u00d7 3) \u00f7 6|=; 30 \u00f7 6|=; 5]"
      },
