        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Compute <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2\\div 8 \\times 12.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Compute [MATH: 2\\div 8 \\times 12.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>When the only operations are multiplication and division, </p><ul><li><p>we carry out the operations from left to right, using parentheses <span class=\"math\">[MATH: (\\cdots)]</span> to make our working clearer, and</p></li><li><p>we can swap the order in which the operations are carried out.</p></li></ul><p>Therefore,</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2 \u00f7 8 \u00d7 12|=; 2 \u00d7 12 \u00f7 8|=; (2 \u00d7 12) \u00f7 8|=; 24 \u00f7 8|=; 3|.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "When the only operations are multiplication and division,\n\n- we carry out the operations from left to right, using parentheses [MATH: (\\cdots)] to make our working clearer, and\n- we can swap the order in which the operations are carried out.\n\nTherefore,\n\n[MATH: 2 \u00f7 8 \u00d7 12|=; 2 \u00d7 12 \u00f7 8|=; (2 \u00d7 12) \u00f7 8|=; 24 \u00f7 8|=; 3|.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nCompute [MATH: 2\\div 8 \\times 12.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWhen the only operations are multiplication and division,\n\n- we carry out the operations from left to right, using parentheses [MATH: (\\cdots)] to make our working clearer, and\n- we can swap the order in which the operations are carried out.\n\nTherefore,\n\n[MATH: 2 \u00f7 8 \u00d7 12|=; 2 \u00d7 12 \u00f7 8|=; (2 \u00d7 12) \u00f7 8|=; 24 \u00f7 8|=; 3|.]"
