          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>When the only operations are multiplication and division, </p><ul><li><p>we carry out the operations from left to right, using parentheses <span class=\"math\">[MATH: (\\cdots)]</span> to make our working clearer, and</p></li><li><p>we can swap the order in which the operations are carried out.</p></li></ul><p>Therefore,</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 24 \u00d7 5 \u00f7 3|=; 24 \u00f7 3 \u00d7 5|=; (24 \u00f7 3) \u00d7 5|=; 8 \u00d7 5|=; 40|.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "When the only operations are multiplication and division,\n\n- we carry out the operations from left to right, using parentheses [MATH: (\\cdots)] to make our working clearer, and\n- we can swap the order in which the operations are carried out.\n\nTherefore,\n\n[MATH: 24 \u00d7 5 \u00f7 3|=; 24 \u00f7 3 \u00d7 5|=; (24 \u00f7 3) \u00d7 5|=; 8 \u00d7 5|=; 40|.]",
