    "readable_text": "Item 1 \u2014 Tutorial: Introduction\n\nContent:\nLet's consider the following expression:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 12\\div 4 \\times 7]\n\nContent:\nNotice that this expression contains multiplication and division. So how do we compute its value?\n\nContent:\nTo help us, we have the following rule:\n\nContent:\n> When an expression contains only multiplication and division, we carry out the operations from left to right.\n\nContent:\nSo, we must first carry out the division [MATH: (12\\div 4).] We can emphasize this using parentheses [MATH: (\\phantom{0}){:}]\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\big(12\\div 4\\big) \\times 7]\n\nContent:\nHere, the parentheses tell us which part of the expression to do first.\n\nContent:\nNow, we evaluate our expression as follows:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: (12 \u00f7 4) \u00d7 7|=; 3 \u00d7 7|=; 21]\n\n---\n\nItem 2 \u2014 Example: Evaluating Expressions With Two Operations\n\nExample Prompt:\nWhat is [MATH: 36\\div 6 \\times 10?]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWhen the only operations are multiplication and division, we carry out the operations from left to right, using parentheses [MATH: (\\cdots)] to make our working clearer:\n\n[MATH: 36 \u00f7 6 \u00d7 10|=; (36 \u00f7 6) \u00d7 10|=; 6 \u00d7 10|=; 60]\n\n---\n\nItem 3 \u2014 Question 1\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: 54 \u00f7 9 \u00d7 8 =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 32]\nb. [MATH: 48]\nc. [MATH: 42]\nd. [MATH: 64]\ne. [MATH: 40]\n\n---\n\nItem 4 \u2014 Question 2\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: 14 \u00d7 2 \u00f7 4 =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 8]\nb. [MATH: 9]\nc. [MATH: 6]\nd. [MATH: 5]\ne. [MATH: 7]\n\n---\n\nItem 5 \u2014 Tutorial: Swapping Multiplication and Division\n\nContent:\nLet's now consider the following expression:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 10{\\color{red}{\\,\\div\\, 6\\,}} {\\color{blue}{\\,\\times\\, 3}}]\n\nContent:\nWe carry out the operations from left to right. However, the division problem is difficult because [MATH: 10] cannot be divided evenly into groups of [MATH: 6.] So, what do we do?\n\nContent:\nTo help us, we have the following rule:\n\nContent:\n> When the only operations are multiplication and division, we can swap the order in which the operations are carried out.\n\nContent:\nTherefore, we can swap the order of the multiplication and division as follows:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 10{\\color{blue}{\\,\\times\\, 3}}{\\color{red}{\\,\\div\\, 6\\,}}]\n\nContent:\nNow, we evaluate our expression:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 10 \u00d7 3 \u00f7 6|=; (10 \u00d7 3) \u00f7 6|=; 30 \u00f7 6|=; 5]\n\n---\n\nItem 6 \u2014 Example: Swapping Multiplication and Division: Division First\n\nExample Prompt:\nCompute [MATH: 2\\div 8 \\times 12.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWhen the only operations are multiplication and division,\n\n- we carry out the operations from left to right, using parentheses [MATH: (\\cdots)] to make our working clearer, and\n- we can swap the order in which the operations are carried out.\n\nTherefore,\n\n[MATH: 2 \u00f7 8 \u00d7 12|=; 2 \u00d7 12 \u00f7 8|=; (2 \u00d7 12) \u00f7 8|=; 24 \u00f7 8|=; 3|.]\n\n---\n\nItem 7 \u2014 Question 3\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: 5 \u00f7 3 \u00d7 6 =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 15]\nb. [MATH: 16]\nc. [MATH: 9]\nd. [MATH: 10]\ne. [MATH: 12]\n\n---\n\nItem 8 \u2014 Question 4\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: 4 \u00f7 3 \u00d7 6 =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 8]\nb. [MATH: 6]\nc. [MATH: 10]\nd. [MATH: 2]\ne. [MATH: 9]\n\n---\n\nItem 9 \u2014 Example: Swapping Multiplication and Division: Multiplication First\n\nExample Prompt:\nFind [MATH: 24\\times 5 \\div 3.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWhen the only operations are multiplication and division,\n\n- we carry out the operations from left to right, using parentheses [MATH: (\\cdots)] to make our working clearer, and\n- we can swap the order in which the operations are carried out.\n\nTherefore,\n\n[MATH: 24 \u00d7 5 \u00f7 3|=; 24 \u00f7 3 \u00d7 5|=; (24 \u00f7 3) \u00d7 5|=; 8 \u00d7 5|=; 40|.]\n\n---\n\nItem 10 \u2014 Question 5\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: 14 \u00d7 8 \u00f7 7 =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 16]\nb. [MATH: 18]\nc. [MATH: 17]\nd. [MATH: 12]\ne. [MATH: 14]\n\n---\n\nItem 11 \u2014 Question 6\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: 12 \u00d7 21 \u00f7 4 =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 63]\nb. [MATH: 84]\nc. [MATH: 53]\nd. [MATH: 64]\ne. [MATH: 68]"
